  <section>
    <h2>What is a Stars giveaway, and why run one?</h2>
    <p>A Stars giveaway is how a channel or group owner splits a pool of Stars among members as prizes, to reward and grow the audience. It runs on the same mechanic as Telegram's older, already-familiar Premium giveaway — the only difference is that winners get Stars credited directly instead of a Premium subscription.</p>
    <p>For channel growth, it's an alternative or complement to <a href="/en/blog/pay-for-telegram-ads-with-stars">Telegram Ads</a>: instead of paying for reach, you reward the audience you already have and give them a reason to boost the channel.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who's eligible to run one?</h2>
    <p>The bar is fairly low: a channel needs at least <strong>50 subscribers</strong>, a group needs at least <strong>500 members</strong>. Anything smaller has to grow to that threshold first.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to set it up, step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check you meet the requirement</strong> — 50+ subscribers for a channel, 500+ members for a group.</li>
      <li><strong>Open the Statistics section</strong> — in a channel: "Channel Settings" &gt; "Statistics" &gt; "Boosts" (in a group: "Group Info" &gt; "Statistics" &gt; "Boosts").</li>
      <li><strong>Choose "Start a Giveaway"</strong> — this opens the setup screen for a new giveaway.</li>
      <li><strong>Set the prize</strong> — enter the total Stars amount and how many winners it's split among.</li>
      <li><strong>Set a deadline and publish</strong> — pick an end date and announce it in the channel.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How are winners actually chosen?</h2>
    <p>A Stars giveaway runs on Telegram's standard <strong>boost-based</strong> selection mechanic — the exact same system already used for Premium giveaways. There's no separate entry form: a member simply boosts the channel or group to take part. Once the giveaway ends, winners are picked at random from everyone who boosted, and the whole process is transparent — anyone can verify the outcome.</p>
  </section>

